  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Feasibility Study - WindGen Village and Commerical and Industrial Minigrids, through WindGen Power USA</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">A USTDA grant to the Ministry of Energy of the Government of Sierra Leone will fund a feasibility study to evaluate the technical, economic, and commercial viability of providing approximately five minigrids for commercial and industrial users (e.g., factories and commercial farms, telecom towers, universities, government buildings) and surrounding communities and approximately 40 minigrids for villages. These minigrids will potentially provide energy access to over 8,600 people, promoting a higher quality of life and economic development. The Study will also create an opportunity for U.S. companies to provide goods, services, and expertise. The Grantee has selected WindGen Power USA, Inc. of Delray Beach, Florida to perform the Study and help implement the Project.</narrative>
  </description>
